''Note: [[Big Stan]] withdrew from the tournament on September 16. His remaining matches (Rounds 6–9) are recorded as forfeit losses, with each opponent receiving two points.''

== Storyline notes ==

* '''Three men, 12 points, one night left.''' Taumafa 12, KAZUKI 12, Takagi 12 — and they close in Toyozawa against Ishida, Diallo, and Ono respectively. The head-to-heads favor Takagi (beat Taumafa) and Taumafa (beat KAZUKI); KAZUKI needs help. The block's soul is decided on the mat in Round 9.
* '''KAZUKI's collapse.''' Three straight losses for the first time since the Fall — Taumafa, Ishida, and now Reyes, the winless man at the bottom. The Shooting Star led the block for five rounds and now needs Diallo in Toyozawa just to stay in the top three. The rebuild is in crisis.
* '''Reyes' first win.''' 1-7, 2 points, and the biggest upset of the tournament: the Cobra Clutch making the man who ended the 1,095-day reign tap. The block's floor is no longer winless.
* '''Ishida's resurrection complete.''' 4-4, 8 points, with Taumafa remaining in Round 9. The television champion's G1 has been the block's best story — four submissions, including KAZUKI, and a winning record now live.
* '''Jusuf and Kuroki: the 10-point chasers.''' Both 5-3, both alive mathematically, both needing help in Toyozawa. The truth-teller closes with Tanaka; the enforcer with Reyes.

